From: Noahcdls <noahcdls@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: codecs: lpass-macros: force runtime suspend across system sleep

The rx, tx, va and wsa macros only have runtime PM ops. When a SoundWire
peripheral stays runtime-active (the WCD9385 is held for jack detection),
the macros it clocks stay active through s2idle and keep their q6prm
votes, so the ADSP keeps LPASS powered and its RPMh DRV ("AUDIO" in the
AOP CXPC violator log) holds CX up for the whole sleep.

Force the runtime suspend across system sleep, so the macro and dcodec
votes that 0064 drops in runtime suspend are dropped for s2idle as well.
Same change as kernel-tb321fu 0019.

Armada 0563 (armada-os/armada 98e87a101559); also 0807 in
ROCKNIX/distribution PR 3636.
---
diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-rx-macro.c b/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-rx-macro.c
index 90d0c5d..1719e32 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-rx-macro.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-rx-macro.c
@@ -4041,6 +4041,7 @@ err_dcodec:
 }
 
 static const struct dev_pm_ops rx_macro_pm_ops = {
+	SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS(pm_runtime_force_suspend, pm_runtime_force_resume)
 	RUNTIME_PM_OPS(rx_macro_runtime_suspend, rx_macro_runtime_resume, NULL)
 };
 
diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-tx-macro.c b/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-tx-macro.c
index f60287d..f3ae25d 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-tx-macro.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-tx-macro.c
@@ -2477,6 +2477,7 @@ err_dcodec:
 }
 
 static const struct dev_pm_ops tx_macro_pm_ops = {
+	SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS(pm_runtime_force_suspend, pm_runtime_force_resume)
 	RUNTIME_PM_OPS(tx_macro_runtime_suspend, tx_macro_runtime_resume, NULL)
 };
 
diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-va-macro.c b/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-va-macro.c
index cd9c689..06910d1 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-va-macro.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-va-macro.c
@@ -1807,6 +1807,7 @@ err_dcodec:
 }
 
 static const struct dev_pm_ops va_macro_pm_ops = {
+	SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS(pm_runtime_force_suspend, pm_runtime_force_resume)
